**Round 7 finding: resolved for this benchmark.** I checked that another article sharing a quote is not attributed, the item’s own answer is found, and multiple matching answers are marked unread.

**Launcher: serious finding.** It checks that the six window-draw folders are new, but does not check the six test-article folders before launching. If a test folder already exists, [launch.sh](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/launch.sh:30) overwrites its log and starts the test runner, which can reuse its old answers when the saved files match. That could make an old or partly old draw appear in the new comparison. The six window draws have already started by then.

The launcher should check **all 12 folders** before starting any draw. None of the 12 target folders currently exists. All 12 listed design hashes passed, and the launcher passed its syntax check. No paid draw was started.